\title{Neighborhood and Local Basis}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{X} be a [topological space](def-000C) and let #{x\in X}. A subset
    #{N\subseteq X} is a \strong{neighborhood} of #{x} if there is an open set
    #{U} such that
    ##{
        x\in U\subseteq N.
    }
    In particular, a neighborhood need \strong{not} itself be open.
}
\p{
    A collection #{\mathcal{B}_x} of neighborhoods of #{x} is a
    \strong{local basis} at #{x} if every neighborhood #{N} of #{x} contains
    some #{B\in\mathcal{B}_x}. A statement holds \strong{locally at #{x}} when
    it holds on some neighborhood of #{x}.
}
